WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.904
The school asks for a first-minute neonatal sequence and correct ventilation and compression coordination. We will connect the actions to the physiology rather than memorize disconnected numbers.
学校要求首分钟新生儿序列及正确通气按压协调。这里把行动连生理，而不是背断开的数字。

00:00:11.904 --> 00:00:23.400
An apneic or gasping newborn needs timely useful breaths after the appropriate initial steps. Sixty seconds is an urgency objective, not a rule to wait for the clock.
适当初步后无呼吸或喘息儿需及时有效呼吸。六十秒是紧迫目标，不是等时钟规则。

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:35.568
The supplied sources contain meaningful conflicts, including old compression thresholds and ratios. Those will be labelled and corrected, not blended into a new hybrid algorithm.
自备来源含重要冲突，包括旧按压阈值比例。需标并纠，不拼成新混合算法。

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:47.952
This session concerns transition at birth. A collapse later in infancy needs its applicable current context and pathway rather than a protocol selected only from the word neonate.
本节关注出生过渡。之后婴儿倒下需按当前情境路径，不能只凭新生儿一词选协议。

00:00:47.952 --> 00:00:58.440
Before birth, oxygen and carbon dioxide exchange occur through the placenta. The umbilical vein carries relatively oxygen-rich blood toward the fetus.
出生前氧及二氧化碳经胎盘交换，脐静脉把相对富氧血送向胎儿。

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:09.480
The two umbilical arteries return blood toward the placenta. Artery and vein describe direction relative to the heart, not a universal high- or low-oxygen rule.
两脐动脉把血送回胎盘。动静脉描述相对心方向，不是通用高低含氧规则。

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:17.088
The fetal lungs are fluid-filled and pulmonary vascular resistance is high. They are not yet the principal gas-exchange route.
胎肺充液且肺血管阻力高，尚非主要气体交换路。

00:01:17.088 --> 00:01:29.784
After birth, effective lung aeration and ventilation become essential. That is why the birth-resuscitation sequence emphasizes breathing before simply adding compressions or medicines.
出生后有效肺充气通气变必要，因此出生复苏强调呼吸，而非只加按压药物。

00:01:29.784 --> 00:01:42.048
The ductus venosus allows a portion of umbilical blood to bypass the liver. Do not describe the fetal liver as receiving no useful flow or the ductus as a direct lung shortcut.
静脉导管让部分脐血绕肝，不能说胎肝无有用血流，也不能把该导管当直接绕肺。

00:01:42.048 --> 00:01:50.952
The foramen ovale provides a route between the right and left atria. The ductus arteriosus connects pulmonary artery and aorta.
卵圆孔提供右左心房间路，动脉导管连接肺动脉及主动脉。

00:01:50.952 --> 00:02:00.600
These latter routes help divert flow away from the high-resistance fetal lung circuit. The direction and amount of flow depend on pressures and resistance.
后两条帮助血流避高阻胎肺循环，流向流量依压力阻力。

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:12.024
Tracing the route is more useful than memorizing three names. Explain which organ is partly bypassed and why the circulation must change after birth.
追路线比只背三名有用，需解释部分绕哪个器官及出生后为何必须改变。

00:02:12.024 --> 00:02:21.264
Effective lung aeration supports oxygen transfer and lowers pulmonary vascular resistance, allowing more blood to reach the pulmonary circulation.
有效肺充气支持氧交换并降肺血管阻力，让更多血入肺循环。

00:02:21.264 --> 00:02:32.280
Removal of the low-resistance placental circulation changes systemic resistance and venous filling. Together, these changes alter the pressures across the fetal shunts.
低阻胎盘循环移除会改全身阻力及静脉充盈，两者共同改变胎分流两侧压力。

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:42.528
Functional closure and later anatomical closure are not identical. Do not teach that every shunt becomes permanently closed at the instant of birth.
功能闭合与后续解剖闭合不同，不能说每条分流出生瞬间就永久闭。

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:56.208
Poor ventilation, hypoxia, acidosis and cold can interfere with successful transition. Supporting breathing and temperature therefore treats linked physiology rather than isolated checkboxes.
通气差、低氧、酸及冷可妨过渡，因此支持呼吸温度是在处理相连生理，不是分离勾选。

00:02:56.208 --> 00:03:09.408
Ask about gestation, multiple fetuses, maternal illness, medicines and delivery complications. Known risk guides preparation, but a baby without risk factors may still need help.
需问孕周、多胎、母病药及分娩并发。已知风险指导准备，但无风险儿仍可能需帮助。

00:03:09.408 --> 00:03:19.728
Name the newborn provider and ensure maternal observation continues. A small crew should recognize competing tasks and request additional resources early.
需点新生儿负责者并保母观察。小车组要识竞争任务并早增援。

00:03:19.728 --> 00:03:29.304
Allocate timing, equipment and communication rather than have everyone reach for the baby at once. Use clear requests and confirm what was done.
需分计时器械沟通，不能所有人同时伸向婴儿；请求需清楚并确认完成。

00:03:29.304 --> 00:03:40.608
Agree cord management and the immediate support plan with other clinicians present, including a midwife when involved. Individual authority and competence still govern each action.
需与在场临床者含助产士一致脐带及即时支持计划，各人授权能力仍约束行动。

00:03:40.608 --> 00:03:50.856
Prepare a safe supported warm area and the appropriate thermal supplies. Do not place an infant on an unstable cold surface while searching for equipment.
需备安全支撑暖区及适当保温，不能把婴放不稳冷面再找器械。

00:03:50.856 --> 00:04:02.904
Verify mask sizes, valve function, pressure monitoring when available and the gas-source arrangement of the actual device. Presence in a sealed kit does not prove readiness.
需核面罩、阀、有时的压监及真实气源安排，密封包中有器械不证明已准备。

00:04:02.904 --> 00:04:15.336
Have suction for obstruction, a clock, auscultation and appropriate oxygenation monitoring. Do not make attachment of every monitor a prerequisite for starting indicated breaths.
需备阻塞吸引、时钟、听诊及适当氧监，但不能把接完全部监测当开始所需呼吸前提。

00:04:15.336 --> 00:04:27.504
Identify authorized backup devices and skilled assistance before difficulty arises. A device that does not fit the newborn or is outside the operator's role is not a usable backup.
困难前需识获准备用及训练协助，不贴合或超操作者权限的器械不是可用备用。

00:04:27.504 --> 00:04:35.904
Record the complete-birth time. Quickly assess gestational context, tone and whether breathing or crying is effective.
需记完整出生时间，并快评孕期背景、张力及呼吸哭是否有效。

00:04:35.904 --> 00:04:46.560
A well baby can receive appropriate observed skin-to-skin care while warmth and ongoing evaluation continue. Good first appearance is not permission to stop watching.
良好婴儿可适当观察下接触，同时保温持续评；首次外观好不允许不再观察。

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:57.216
Poor tone, absent breathing or other concern leads to the appropriate initial-support branch. Do not spend the first minute calculating a complete Apgar before acting.
张力差、无呼吸或其他担忧需入相应初始支持，不能首分钟只算完整Apgar才动。

00:04:57.216 --> 00:05:08.400
Begin assessing heart rate and prepare ventilation as indicated. The questions organize the response; they do not replace direct examination or the full current algorithm.
需开始评心率并按需备通气；问题组织反应，却不替直接检查或完整现行算法。

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:18.432
Evaporation removes heat as water leaves wet skin. For the appropriate routine newborn, drying and replacing wet material reduce that loss.
水离湿皮时蒸发带热。适当常规新生儿擦干及换湿物可减失。

00:05:18.432 --> 00:05:30.504
Convection involves cooler air, especially drafts, while conduction involves direct contact with a cold surface. Warm the area and prepare a suitable supported surface.
对流涉及冷空气尤其风，传导是直接碰冷表面。需暖环境及备合适支撑面。

00:05:30.504 --> 00:05:41.664
Radiation transfers heat toward nearby cooler objects even without contact. A baby can lose heat despite lying on a warm blanket if the surroundings remain cold.
辐射即使无接触也向附近冷物传热，周围冷时即使躺暖毯仍可失热。

00:05:41.664 --> 00:05:55.032
Cold stress increases metabolic demand and can worsen oxygen and glucose balance. The mechanism explains why thermal protection must continue through transfer, not only immediately after birth.
冷应激增代谢并可恶化氧糖平衡，故保温需贯穿转移，不仅出生即刻。

00:05:55.032 --> 00:06:08.664
Current M zero nine uses an axillary range of thirty-six point five to thirty-seven point five degrees Celsius. Keep this separate from the older L zero two and textbook temperature wording.
现行M09腋范围三十六点五至三十七点五摄氏度，需与旧L02及教材措辞分开。

00:06:08.664 --> 00:06:23.208
A routine term baby needs appropriate drying, removal of wet material, covering and observation. Very preterm care can require wrapping without the same drying sequence; use the trained gestation-specific plan.
常规足月需适当擦干、除湿物、覆盖及观察；极早产可能需不同擦干顺序包膜，应依训练孕期计划。

00:06:23.208 --> 00:06:34.728
If a thermal bag or wrap is used, keep the face and airway accessible and do not secure it around the neck. Monitor temperature and the ongoing clinical condition.
用保温袋膜时需脸及气道可及，不扎颈，并监温及临床。

00:06:34.728 --> 00:06:47.736
Avoid direct unregulated heat and hot-water bottles. Do not initiate therapeutic cooling from this teaching; specialized cooling decisions do not replace prevention of accidental hypothermia.
需避未控直热热水袋，也不能据本课开始治疗降温。专业降温不替预防意外低温。

00:06:47.736 --> 00:06:58.272
Perform appropriate warmth and positioning promptly. Avoid a flexed chin or excessive neck extension and check that support actually helps airway patency.
需迅速保温摆位，避下巴过屈或颈过伸，并核支持真改善通畅。

00:06:58.272 --> 00:07:08.016
Use gentle stimulation such as appropriate drying or rubbing the back. Do not slap, shake or repeatedly apply harsh sole stimulation.
可适当擦干轻揉背，不能打摇或反复粗暴弹脚。

00:07:08.016 --> 00:07:15.984
Clear visible obstruction with the appropriate method when needed, not as an obligatory routine before every first breath.
需要时可适当清可见阻塞，不是每次首呼吸前必做常规。

00:07:15.984 --> 00:07:26.184
Then act on breathing and heart rate without delay. Continuing stimulation for another long cycle is not the answer to persistent apnea or gasping.
之后需即依呼吸心率行动。持续无呼吸喘息时，再长一轮刺激不是答案。

00:07:26.184 --> 00:07:34.296
Initial warmth and evaluation can occur during deferred cord clamping. The team should agree the plan before birth when possible.
延迟结扎时可初保温评估，可行时全队应出生前一致计划。

00:07:34.296 --> 00:07:44.040
The current pages use different timing language, as explained in the birth session. Keep vigorous-infant care and a newborn needing immediate support distinct.
现行页面时间措辞不同，已在分娩节解释。需区分有活力儿及需即时支持者。

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:54.480
Do not let a timer prevent effective breaths. If required care cannot be provided with the cord intact, coordinate the appropriate operational action rather than delay.
不能让秒表阻止有效呼吸。完整脐带状态不能提供所需照护时，应协调适当操作而非延误。

00:07:54.480 --> 00:08:05.136
Do not introduce cord milking, a compulsory below-placenta position or a claimed half-blood-loss rule from unqualified old text. Use the actual trained plan.
不能从未限定旧文引入挤脐、强制低于胎盘位或所谓一半血丢失规则，需真实训练计划。

00:08:05.136 --> 00:08:16.800
Current professional guidance does not recommend routine suction merely because fluid is clear or meconium-stained. A nonvigorous baby still needs the breathing problem addressed promptly.
现行专业指导不建议仅因液清或胎粪染就常规吸，无活力儿仍需迅速处理呼吸问题。

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:29.064
If the airway appears obstructed, use appropriate authorized clearing and reassess. Obstruction may involve secretions or other material, but not every poor breath is a suction problem.
气道似阻时需适当授权清并复评。阻可为分泌或他物，但不是每次差呼吸都要吸。

00:08:29.064 --> 00:08:41.448
The local M zero nine body and older Nancy text include broader or contradictory meconium wording. Do not use that as permission for prolonged routine suction before useful ventilation.
当地M09及旧Nancy含更宽或矛盾胎粪措辞，不能据此在有效通气前长常规吸。

00:08:41.448 --> 00:08:52.464
Use the current operational instruction and appropriately trained help if uncertainty persists. Airway clearing must improve ventilation rather than become the task that prevents it.
不确定持续时需现行操作指令及训练帮助。清理必须改善通气，不能变成阻碍通气的任务。

00:08:52.464 --> 00:09:01.776
Assess heart rate promptly and report it to the team. Initial precordial auscultation is useful while appropriate monitoring is arranged.
需迅速评心率并报团队，安排监测时初始心前听诊有用。

00:09:01.776 --> 00:09:14.016
ECG can provide a rapid rate, while pulse oximetry also contributes oxygenation information. A poor or delayed probe signal should not stop an urgent ventilation decision.
ECG可快给率，血氧可补氧合。探头信号差或慢不应阻止急通气决定。

00:09:14.016 --> 00:09:24.168
An electrical rate is not itself proof of mechanical output or adequate oxygenation. Combine it with actual clinical response and relevant findings.
电率本身不证明机械输出或氧合充分，需结合临床反应与发现。

00:09:24.168 --> 00:09:34.896
Do not spend a full minute searching for a perfect count while an apneic newborn remains unsupported. Use the best reliable timely method and reassess.
不能为完美计数找整分钟，让无呼吸婴无支持。需最佳可靠及时方法并复评。

00:09:34.896 --> 00:09:45.216
After appropriate initial steps, apnea, gasping or a persistent heart rate below one hundred requires assisted ventilation through the current newborn pathway.
适当初步后，无呼吸、喘息或持续心率低于一百，需按现行新生儿路径辅助通气。

00:09:45.216 --> 00:09:53.424
Do not wait for a twenty-second pause to satisfy the old apnea definition. Inadequate breathing is an action finding now.
不能等满二十秒停顿才符合旧呼吸暂停定义，呼吸不足现在就是行动发现。

00:09:53.424 --> 00:10:04.632
The aim is prompt effective ventilation, not merely starting to squeeze a bag before a timer expires. Ensure useful air entry and reassess the response.
目标是迅速有效通气，不只是秒表前开始挤囊。需确保有用气流并复评。

00:10:04.632 --> 00:10:13.920
Apgar scoring and every monitor attachment are secondary to indicated support. The score can be documented alongside ongoing care.
Apgar及接全监测都次于所需支持，评分可在持续照护中记录。

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:24.480
The school outline and supplied textbook teach forty to sixty breaths per minute for newborn ventilation. The inspected current BCEHS algorithm prints thirty to sixty.
学校周纲及自备教材教新生儿每分四十至六十吹，所检现行BCEHS算法印三十至六十。

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:36.312
Keep the school rehearsal requirement visible and verify the assessed version with the instructor while recognizing the current operational range. Do not silently relabel one as the other.
需保学校演练要求，并与教师核考核版，同时认识现行操作范围，不能悄悄把一者改标另一者。

00:10:36.312 --> 00:10:46.440
Use a controlled rhythm with effective breaths and appropriate release. A rate within a range does not prove useful ventilation if there is leak or obstruction.
需受控节律、有效呼吸及适当释放。有漏阻时，频率在范围内不证明通气有用。

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:56.952
Compression coordination and older-child rescue breathing are different situations. Announce the algorithm and branch so the team does not mix its numbers.
按压协调及较大儿童救援呼吸属不同情境，需说算法分支，避免全队混数字。

00:10:56.952 --> 00:11:07.656
Choose the appropriate mask size and fit rather than cover the eyes or rely on a poorly fitting edge. Use the actual device instructions and trained technique.
需选合适面罩贴合，不盖眼或依漏边，并用真实说明训练技术。

00:11:07.656 --> 00:11:16.392
Maintain an open supported airway. Too much neck extension, flexion or pressure into soft tissues can worsen the problem.
需维持通畅有支撑气道。颈过伸屈或压软组织可恶化。

00:11:16.392 --> 00:11:25.008
Use a trained two-provider approach when it improves positioning and seal, allocating bag operation separately from airway support.
可改善摆位密封时应训练双人方法，把挤囊与气道支持分开。

00:11:25.008 --> 00:11:33.984
Observe the actual breath effect. A correctly held-looking mask with no useful inflation is not a completed ventilation task.
需看真实效果。面罩拿得像对但无有效充气，不算完成通气。

00:11:33.984 --> 00:11:44.808
A self-inflating bag and a flow-inflating system do not work in the same way. Know which device is actually in your hands and what it needs to deliver a breath.
自充囊与流充系统工作不同，需知道手中真实器械及提供呼吸所需。

00:11:44.808 --> 00:11:57.000
A self-inflating bag can provide air ventilation without an oxygen source, while other systems need the appropriate gas supply. That does not mean every bag gives effective free-flow oxygen.
自充囊可无氧源做空气通气，其他系统需合适气源。但不代表每囊都有效提供自由流氧。

00:11:57.000 --> 00:12:10.296
Check oxygen concentration arrangements, valves and pressure-monitoring controls according to the actual device. Do not assume a reservoir or connected tubing establishes a known delivered concentration.
需依真实器械核氧浓度安排、阀及压监控制，不能认储氧袋或接管就证明已知输送浓度。

00:12:10.296 --> 00:12:21.264
Practise setup and failure recognition on the available equipment. This explanation does not certify an uninspected model or justify overriding its safety features.
需在可用器械练设置及故障识别。本解释不认证未检型号，也不允许压过安全特性。

00:12:21.264 --> 00:12:32.112
Look for useful chest movement and a rising heart rate after assisted breaths. The physiological response is more important than the number of times a bag was squeezed.
辅助呼吸后需看有用胸动及心率升，生理反应比挤囊次数重要。

00:12:32.112 --> 00:12:44.400
If heart rate does not rise, reassess ventilation quality and the clinical situation. Leak, airway position, obstruction or equipment failure can prevent lung inflation.
率不升需复评通气质量及情境，漏、头位、阻塞或器械故障均可阻充气。

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:54.216
Thirty seconds of ineffective bagging does not equal thirty seconds of ventilation that inflated the lungs. Do not progress simply because time passed.
三十秒无效挤囊不等于三十秒能充肺的通气，不能只因时间过就进阶。

00:12:54.216 --> 00:13:03.792
Reassess after each correction while requesting help as needed. Continued poor response can also reflect other pathology that needs advanced evaluation.
每次纠正后需复查并按需求助，持续差反应也可有需高级评估的其他病理。

00:13:03.792 --> 00:13:14.040
The actual linked BCEHS corrective table begins with mask adjustment and repositioning. These address common causes of leak and ineffective airway alignment.
实际BCEHS纠正表先调面罩及重新摆位，处理常见漏气及气道对线无效。

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:24.504
A trained two-hand seal may help while another provider operates the bag. Keep the airway neutral or slightly extended rather than force it into an extreme position.
训练双手密封可由另一人挤囊，需中立轻伸而非强极端位。

00:13:24.504 --> 00:13:34.176
After those corrections, provide breaths and reassess movement and heart-rate response. The table explicitly includes a reassessment point.
纠后需呼吸并复查胸动及率反应，表明确有复评点。

00:13:34.176 --> 00:13:44.232
Do not perform every later step automatically when the first correction works. The purpose is effective ventilation, not completion of a mnemonic.
首改有效时，不应自动做所有后步。目标是有效通气，不是完成记忆法。

00:13:44.232 --> 00:13:55.344
If obstruction is suspected, use appropriate clearing of mouth and nose within the actual procedure. Suction is not required solely because the letter S appears in the mnemonic.
疑阻时可依真实程序清口鼻。不能只因记忆法有S就必须吸。

00:13:55.344 --> 00:14:04.800
Opening the mouth and supporting the jaw can improve the airway through the trained method. Avoid compressing soft tissues or causing unnecessary trauma.
依训练开口支持颌可改善气道，需避压软组织或多余伤。

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:14.856
Try ventilation again and check the effect before further escalation. Communicate what changed and whether useful inflation or rate response occurred.
进一步升级前需再试通气查效果，并报改了什么、有无有效充气率反应。

00:14:14.856 --> 00:14:24.984
Unnecessary repeated suction can delay ventilation and worsen bradycardia or injury. Stay focused on the actual barrier and the newborn's response.
多余反复吸可延误通气并恶化慢率伤，需聚焦真实障碍及反应。

00:14:24.984 --> 00:14:38.064
The local MR.SOPA pressure row prints increments of five to ten centimeters of water and a maximum of forty. Identify that as the table's corrective reference, not a routine starting prescription.
当地MR.SOPA压行印每次五至十厘米水及最高四十，需识为该纠正表参考，不是常规起始处方。

00:14:38.064 --> 00:14:49.824
Actual pressure use requires the correct device, monitoring, gestational context and trained pathway. The aim is effective lung inflation with the least harmful suitable pressure.
真实压使用需正确器械监测、孕期及训练路径，目标是以最少适当伤害的压有效充肺。

00:14:49.824 --> 00:14:59.976
Do not cover a pop-off valve or repeatedly increase force merely because the old textbook describes it. Excess volume and pressure can injure the lung.
不能因旧教材描述就压泄压阀或反复加力，量压过大可伤肺。

00:14:59.976 --> 00:15:10.512
Check for an unresolved leak, obstruction or system problem and seek appropriate help. Pressure escalation cannot compensate for every failure mode.
需查未解漏阻或系统问题并求适当帮助，加压不能代所有故障处理。

00:15:10.512 --> 00:15:22.632
When useful ventilation cannot be established, an appropriate alternative airway may be needed. Arrange the right trained resource rather than persist indefinitely with ineffective breaths.
无法建立有效通气时可需合适替代气道。需安排正确训练资源，而非无限无效吹。

00:15:22.632 --> 00:15:34.128
Current M zero nine lists supraglottic airway and PEEP in the PCP section, but actual device fit, eligibility, training and procedure requirements still apply.
现行M09在PCP栏列声门上气道及PEEP，但真实贴合、资格、训练及程序仍需满足。

00:15:34.128 --> 00:15:44.664
Intubation and specialized neonatal support remain separate level-dependent actions. A diagram that says intubate does not authorize every person who reads it.
插管及专业婴支持仍依不同层级，图写插管不授权每位读者。

00:15:44.664 --> 00:15:56.040
After any device change, verify useful ventilation and reassess. A placed airway is not automatically a functioning airway, especially after movement.
换器械后需核有效通气并复评，置入不自动代表有效，尤其移动后。

00:15:56.040 --> 00:16:09.552
A term newborn starting assisted ventilation is not automatically given one hundred percent oxygen. The current local initial-resuscitation instruction uses room air with saturation-guided adjustment.
足月开始辅助通气不自动100%氧，现行当地初始指令为空气并依血氧调整。

00:16:09.552 --> 00:16:20.184
Use the appropriate right-hand or wrist preductal probe and verify a reliable signal. Saturation and heart-rate measurements answer different questions.
需适当右手腕导管前探头并核可靠信号，血氧与率回答不同问题。

00:16:20.184 --> 00:16:32.544
Prematurity can change oxygen requirements; do not infer one concentration for every gestation. Follow the actual trained local plan and seek suitable neonatal support.
早产可改氧需求，不能所有孕期同浓度，需真实训练当地计划及合适新生儿支持。

00:16:32.544 --> 00:16:45.288
The compression branch uses one hundred percent oxygen in the current algorithm, followed by appropriate titration when compressions are no longer needed. Do not transplant that phase into all routine birth care.
现行算法按压分支用100%氧，不再需按压后适当调低，不能把该阶段搬到所有常规出生照护。

00:16:45.288 --> 00:16:54.456
The inspected current algorithm gives sixty-five to seventy percent at two minutes and seventy to seventy-five at three minutes after birth.
所检现行算法列出生后二分六十五至七十、三分七十至七十五。

00:16:54.456 --> 00:17:03.576
At four minutes it lists seventy-five to eighty, at five minutes eighty to eighty-five, and at ten minutes eighty-five to ninety-five percent.
四分列七十五至八十、五分八十至八十五、十分八十五至九十五。

00:17:03.576 --> 00:17:14.616
These timed targets explain why a newly born infant does not instantly need an adult ninety-four-percent target. Do not use them to excuse apnea or failing ventilation.
定时目标解释为何刚出生不立刻需成人九十四目标，但不能用它原谅无呼吸或通气失败。

00:17:14.616 --> 00:17:27.336
Use the actual algorithm and reliable monitoring, with clinical response. Do not extrapolate an unprinted exact value between every minute or treat a noisy number as adequate oxygenation.
需真实算法、可靠监测及临床反应，不能对每分另推未印准确值，也不能把噪声数当充分氧合。

00:17:27.336 --> 00:17:36.096
Current birth guidance adds compressions when heart rate remains below sixty after thirty seconds of ventilation that effectively inflates the lungs.
现行出生指导在能有效充肺的三十秒通气后，率仍低于六十才加按压。

00:17:36.096 --> 00:17:49.152
Optimize ventilation, including an appropriate alternative airway when feasible and authorized. Ineffective bagging time must not be mistaken for the required useful ventilation interval.
需优化通气，可行获准时含合适替代气道。不能把无效挤囊时间错当所需有效区间。

00:17:49.152 --> 00:18:08.208
The June twenty twenty-six comparison uses a below-one-hundred compression gate. The recovered March twenty twenty-five copy instead prints below sixty at all three staged gates, which can delay ventilation earlier. Neither dated loop replaces the current ventilation and compression decisions.
2026年6月比较版把低于100作为按压门槛；找回的2025年3月副本则在三个分阶段门槛均写低于60，可能在早期延误通气。两份有日期的循环，都不能替代现行独立的通气和按压判断。

00:18:08.208 --> 00:18:19.296
The original diagram emphasizes the separate decision gates. It is a reasoning aid, not a complete device procedure or permission to bypass the current full algorithm.
原创图强调独立决定门，是推理辅助，不是完整器械程序，也不允许跳过现行完整算法。

00:18:19.296 --> 00:18:28.224
Practise the two-thumb encircling technique on the actual training manikin, supporting the torso with the fingers while thumbs compress the sternum.
需在真实训练人偶练双拇指环抱，以手指支躯体、拇指压胸骨。

00:18:28.224 --> 00:18:37.728
Use the lower third of the sternum while avoiding the xiphoid. Do not select a lower landmark solely from the nipple line or press into the upper abdomen.
需胸骨下三分之一避剑突，不能只凭乳线选低标志或压上腹。

00:18:37.728 --> 00:18:48.984
Aim for about one third of the chest anterior-posterior diameter, allow full recoil and avoid leaning. Exact practical positioning needs instructor observation.
目标约胸前后径三分之一，需全回弹及不倚压，准确实操位需教师观察。

00:18:48.984 --> 00:18:59.184
The old two-finger illustration is not the preferred birth technique taught here. Compression quality and synchronized effective ventilation must be assessed together.
旧双指图不是这里教的首选出生法，需把按压质量及同步有效通气一起评。

00:18:59.184 --> 00:19:09.168
The school and current newborn pathway use three compressions synchronized to one ventilation. Practise a coordinated four-event cycle with the team.
学校及现行新生儿路径用三压同步一吹，需全队练协调四事件周期。

00:19:09.168 --> 00:19:20.112
The goal is ninety compressions and thirty breaths per minute: one hundred twenty total events. That does not mean one hundred twenty compressions plus extra breaths.
目标每分九十压及三十吹，共一百二十事件，不是一百二十压外加吹。

00:19:20.112 --> 00:19:33.888
The supplied Nancy paragraph mixes this newborn context with thirty-to-two, fifteen-to-two and one hundred to one hundred twenty compressions. Do not practise those mixed instructions as birth resuscitation.
自备Nancy段把该背景与三十比二、十五比二及一百至一百二十压混合，不能练成出生复苏。

00:19:33.888 --> 00:19:45.960
Maintain useful breaths, recoil and communication, and minimize unnecessary interruptions. A memorized count without depth and ventilation effect is not adequate performance.
需有效吹、回弹沟通并少不必要中断，只有计数无深度通气效果不算合格表现。

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:56.904
After the coordinated support interval, reassess heart rate and clinical response using the current pathway. Do not stop useful care for an unnecessarily long count.
协调支持区间后需依现行路径复评率及临床，不能为多余长计数停有效照护。

00:19:56.904 --> 00:20:08.112
A heart rate of eighty is above the compression threshold but still below one hundred. Compressions may stop while effective ventilation continues, depending on the actual findings.
率八十高于按压门槛却仍低于一百，依真实发现可停按压而继续有效通气。

00:20:08.112 --> 00:20:18.888
Even a rate above one hundred does not establish adequate spontaneous breathing. Continue or reduce support according to breathing and the full response, not rate alone.
即使率超过一百也不证明自发呼吸足。需依呼吸及全反应继续或减支持，不能只看率。

00:20:18.888 --> 00:20:31.368
Persistent severe bradycardia needs verification of effective ventilation and compressions and appropriate advanced escalation. Do not repeatedly cycle through ineffective actions.
持续重慢需核有效通气按压并适当高级升级，不能反复循环无效动作。

00:20:31.368 --> 00:20:43.632
If heart rate remains below sixty despite sixty seconds of coordinated compressions and adequate ventilation, the current framework calls for advanced escalation including medicine consideration.
六十秒协调按压及足够通气后仍低于六十，现行框架需高级升级含药物考虑。

00:20:43.632 --> 00:20:55.104
Current M zero nine places vascular access, intubation and epinephrine beyond the PCP operational section, with specialized umbilical access separately restricted.
现行M09将通路、插管及肾上腺素置于PCP操作栏之外，脐通路另有限制。

00:20:55.104 --> 00:21:07.416
Do not give an algorithm-box dose or assume a term baby exceeds a weight limit. Actual eligibility, reliable weight, device suitability and the appropriate provider are required.
不能只按算法框给量，也不能认足月必超过体重线。需真实资格、可靠重、适合器械及适当提供者。

00:21:07.416 --> 00:21:19.896
Continue effective basic support while the team considers other causes such as blood loss or pneumothorax. This session does not prescribe a PCP neonatal infusion or invasive rescue procedure.
团队考虑失血气胸等时，仍需有效基本支持。本节不开PCP新生儿输注或侵入救援处方。

00:21:19.896 --> 00:21:33.072
After response, continue frequent appropriate observation of breathing, rate, oxygenation and responsiveness. A single cry or improved number does not establish sustained recovery.
反应后仍需频繁适当观察呼吸率氧合反应，一哭或数字好转不证明持续恢复。

00:21:33.072 --> 00:21:43.008
Maintain suitable thermal protection and check devices after movement. Support that worked on the birth surface may become displaced during transfer.
需适当保温并移动后查器械，在出生面有效的支持可转移后移位。

00:21:43.008 --> 00:21:54.000
Watch for recurrent apnea, worsening effort, poor perfusion or altered tone. Reassess the whole situation rather than assume the original problem cannot recur.
需看反复停呼吸、用力恶化、灌注差或张力变，不能认原问题绝不再发。

00:21:54.000 --> 00:22:04.320
Arrange the appropriate receiving center, resources and notification. Do not use a reassuring Apgar or a complete cord cut as a discharge decision.
需安排适当接收中心资源预警，不能用放心Apgar或已剪脐当出院决定。

00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:18.240
Consider neonatal glucose in the relevant illness, feeding, temperature and gestational context through the applicable pathway. Not every healthy term baby needs routine screening immediately after birth.
需依相关病、喂养、温及孕期通过适用路径考虑血糖，不是每个健康足月儿刚出都需常规筛。

00:22:18.240 --> 00:22:30.576
The school outline incorrectly generalizes a neonatal two-point-six threshold to children older than one month. The pediatric lecture distinguishes that from the current general below-four pathway.
学校错误地把新生儿二点六推广至一月以上儿童，儿科节已与现行一般低于四路径区分。

00:22:30.576 --> 00:22:44.280
A neonatal D ten infusion described in a book or advanced protocol does not give PCP independent neonatal IV authority. Check the actual provider, age, route and consultation requirements.
书或高级协议写新生儿D10输注，不授权PCP独立新生儿静脉。需核提供者、年龄、途径及会诊。

00:22:44.280 --> 00:22:56.640
Feeding requires a safe clinical condition and effective airway protection. Do not put milk or glucose into an inadequately responsive or poorly breathing baby as a substitute for urgent support.
喂养需安全状态及有效气道保护，不能把奶糖放反应呼吸差婴来替急支持。

00:22:56.640 --> 00:23:08.016
Tell the family in clear short language that the baby needs help breathing or circulation support and what the team is doing now. Avoid a technical score as the whole explanation.
需用短清语言说婴需呼吸或循环帮助及团队正在做什么，不能只用技术分数解释。

00:23:08.016 --> 00:23:16.872
Maintain privacy and appropriate family involvement while preserving space for effective care. Assign a communicator when personnel allow.
需保隐私及适当家属参与，同时保有效照护空间，人员许可时专人沟通。

00:23:16.872 --> 00:23:26.592
Do not promise a normal outcome or announce permanent disability from a low early score. A population association is not an individual prediction.
不能保证正常结局，也不能凭早低分宣布永久残疾，人群关联不是个人预测。

00:23:26.592 --> 00:23:37.224
Do not use a ten-minute old-text passage or a clock alone to terminate care. Follow current guidance and consultation with clinical context and family participation.
不能以旧十分段或单纯时钟终止，需现行指导会诊、临床背景及家属参与。

00:23:37.224 --> 00:23:49.296
In this original case, a newborn at an estimated thirty-nine weeks and one day has poor tone, gasping and an auscultated heart rate of eighty after appropriate initial steps.
原创例为估三十九周一天，适当初步后张力差、喘息及听诊率八十。

00:23:49.296 --> 00:24:00.864
State the current problem: breathing is ineffective and heart rate is below one hundred. Initiate useful assisted ventilation through the current pathway without waiting for Apgar.
需说当前问题为呼吸无效、率低于一百，并依现行路径开始有效辅助通气，不等Apgar。

00:24:00.864 --> 00:24:10.560
Maintain the thermal and maternal-care roles while another provider assists ventilation and monitoring. A birth emergency still involves both patients.
需维持保温及母体角色，同时另一人协助通气监测，出生急症仍涉及双方。

00:24:10.560 --> 00:24:22.248
Do not begin compressions solely because eighty is below the old page-forty-four one-hundred gate. Use the actual effective-ventilation and persistent-sixty decision process.
不能因八十低于旧44页一百门就按压，需真实有效通气及持续六十门过程。

00:24:22.248 --> 00:24:34.512
Assume early breaths produce little chest movement and an audible mask leak, with the rate still around eighty. State the limitation rather than call this successful ventilation.
假设早吹少胸动且有漏声，率仍约八十。需说明限制，不称成功通气。

00:24:34.512 --> 00:24:43.632
Correct mask fit and airway position using the trained approach, with help for the seal where appropriate. Then give breaths and reassess.
需以训练法改贴合及气道位，适当时协助密封，之后再呼吸复查。

00:24:43.632 --> 00:24:53.664
Do not advance solely because a timer says thirty seconds passed. No useful inflation means the effective-ventilation interval has not been demonstrated.
不能只因秒表过三十就进阶，无有效充气代表有效区间尚未证明。

00:24:53.664 --> 00:25:05.232
Continue the correction pathway and call appropriate help if ventilation remains ineffective. The case tests cause, intervention and measured response, not mnemonic speed.
仍无效需继续纠正并求适当帮助。例检验原因、干预及测反应，不是背字母速度。

00:25:05.232 --> 00:25:15.024
Now assume an improved seal produces useful chest movement, heart rate rises to one hundred thirty-two and spontaneous breathing becomes effective.
现假设改善密封后有用胸动，率升一百三十二，自发呼吸变有效。

00:25:15.024 --> 00:25:22.944
That response supports the importance of ventilation. It does not justify adding compressions because the original rate was eighty.
此反应支持通气重要，不能因原率八十就补加按压。

00:25:22.944 --> 00:25:34.656
Reassess breathing, reliable oxygenation, tone and temperature and adjust support through the current pathway. Do not stop needed support solely because one number improved.
需复评呼吸、可靠氧合、张力及温，并依路径调支持，不能只因一个数改善就停所需支持。

00:25:34.656 --> 00:25:45.144
Record times, corrections and responses and arrange indicated post-resuscitation assessment. The newborn remains a separate patient needing continued care.
需记时间、纠正及反应，并安排所需复苏后评估，婴仍独立需持续照护。

00:25:45.144 --> 00:25:57.360
For an alternative original branch, assume thirty seconds of effective ventilation has been demonstrated but heart rate remains fifty. That meets the current compression decision context.
另一原创分支假设已证三十秒有效通气，但率仍五十，才符合现行按压情境。

00:25:57.360 --> 00:26:09.552
Provide trained synchronized three-to-one support, compression-phase oxygen and appropriate airway/advanced resource planning. Verify both compression and breath quality.
需训练同步三比一、按压期氧及适当气道高级资源计划，并核压吹质量。

00:26:09.552 --> 00:26:20.064
After the coordinated interval, assume rate rises to eighty. Stop compressions as indicated by the current pathway while continuing the ventilation still needed.
协调区间后假率升八十，需依现行路径适应性停压，并继续仍需通气。

00:26:20.064 --> 00:26:31.680
If instead it remains below sixty after adequate coordinated support, escalate with the appropriate advanced team. Do not infer a PCP drug or IO permission from this case.
若足够协调后仍低六十，需适当高级升级，不能从例推PCP药或IO权限。

00:26:31.680 --> 00:26:42.000
Give estimated gestation, birth context and relevant maternal concerns, with source reliability. Distinguish the baby's record from the maternal record.
需给估孕周、出生背景及母担忧，并标来源可靠性，婴与母记录分开。

00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:52.920
State birth time, initial breathing and heart rate, when effective ventilation was achieved and whether compressions were needed. Do not report only bagging started.
需说出生、初呼吸率、何时达到有效通气及是否需压，不能只报开始挤囊。

00:26:52.920 --> 00:27:04.272
Report response, oxygen context, thermal findings, support and timed Apgar observations. Note which readings were reliable and which remained uncertain.
需报反应、氧背景、温、支持及定时Apgar，并分可靠值及未知。

00:27:04.272 --> 00:27:13.800
Finish with current needs and the coordinated receiving plan. A clear trajectory is more useful than a list of actions without their effects.
最后需当前需求及协调接收计划，清趋势比无效果行动清单有用。

00:27:13.800 --> 00:27:24.456
For the first-minute drill, identify the birth clock and demonstrate the initial steps without delaying indicated ventilation. Explain how you know a breath worked.
首分钟演练需识出生时钟并示初步，不延误所需通气，且说明如何知道一吹有效。

00:27:24.456 --> 00:27:35.496
For corrective ventilation, change one problem at a time where feasible and reassess. Do not claim success because all MR.SOPA letters were recited.
纠正时可行尽量一次改一问题并复评，不能因背全MR.SOPA就称成功。

00:27:35.496 --> 00:27:47.880
For the compression branch, demonstrate the current threshold context, technique, three-to-one rhythm and response-driven next step. State why the old mixed ratios are not being used.
按压分支需演现行阈值背景、技术、三比一及反应导下一步，并说为何不用旧混比。

00:27:47.880 --> 00:28:00.000
Instructor observation on the actual training equipment is required for practical signoff. This course prepares the reasoning and sequence but does not certify hands-on resuscitation.
实操签核需教师在真实训练器械上观察。本课准备推理及顺序，但不认证实体复苏。

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:11.064
You should explain why lung aeration changes circulation and why warmth protects oxygen and glucose balance. Mechanism makes the sequence easier to remember correctly.
需解释肺充气如何改循环、保温为何护氧糖。机制能使顺序更易准确记。

00:28:11.064 --> 00:28:19.608
Provide timely useful breaths, test corrections and recognize when the persistent-below-sixty branch requires synchronized support.
需及时有效吹、检纠正，并识持续低六十何时需同步支持。

00:28:19.608 --> 00:28:28.704
Keep the school forty-to-sixty rate, current thirty-to-sixty rate, three-to-one compression sequence and older-child rescue breathing distinct.
需分学校四十至六十、现行三十至六十、三比一按压及较大儿童救援呼吸。

00:28:28.704 --> 00:28:42.216
Then maintain observation, communicate honestly and arrange appropriate care. The accompanying readings identify source conflicts and unresolved school-page locators without pretending they are complete.
之后需持续观察、如实沟通并安排合适照护。配套阅读指出来源冲突及未解学校页，不假装已完整。

00:28:42.216 --> 00:29:21.744
The literal M10 opening distinguishes surfactant-related RDS, retained lung fluid in TTN, infection and air leak. These are possible mechanisms, not a diagnosis from gestational age or a reason to wait for a described72-hour course. Its later-neonatal saturation examples and specialist oxygen/ventilator settings are not first-minute targets or a PCP equipment recipe. Assess breathing effectiveness and deterioration, support within the actual pathway and obtain appropriate help; do not seek a printed high opening pressure with a hand-held bag.
实际M10开头区分与表面活性物质有关的RDS、TTN肺液潴留、感染及漏气。这些是可能机制，不能仅凭孕周诊断，也不能为了书写的72小时病程而等待。其较后新生儿阶段血氧示例及专科氧疗或呼吸机设置，不是出生首分钟目标，也不是PCP器械配方。应评估呼吸有效性和恶化，依真实路径支持并取得适当帮助，不能用手动囊追求印刷的高开放压。

00:29:21.744 --> 00:30:00.720
Original contrast: a four-day-old has poor feeding, grunting and less interaction than usual. The family recalls that low saturations can be normal immediately after birth. That birth-minute table cannot reassure this later presentation. Perform the primary assessment, verify measurement quality without delaying indicated support, protect temperature and communicate the age in days, baseline change, breathing/perfusion findings and response. An apparently term birth or a previous normal check does not exclude infection, congenital disease or another current threat.
原创对照：一名四日龄婴儿进食差、呻吟，并比平时更少互动。家属记得刚出生时较低血氧可能正常，但出生分钟表不能让这次较后发生的表现变得安全。应做初步评估，复核测量质量但不延误有指征的支持，保护体温，并交接日龄、基线变化、呼吸灌注发现及反应。看似足月出生或先前检查正常，不能排除感染、先天疾病或其他当前威胁。

00:30:00.720 --> 00:30:43.704
The recovered March2025 page44 differs materially from the June2026 comparison: its three progression gates all say below60, while the later copy says below100. Neither staged loop should replace the current algorithm. The2025 first gate could withhold useful ventilation from an apneic baby or a persistently slow rate of60-99; the2026 later gate could add compressions too early at those rates. Current birth guidance separates assisted ventilation for apnea/gasping or persistent rate below100 from compressions for persistent below60 after effective ventilation and correction.
找回的2025年3月第44页与2026年6月比较版有实质差异：前者三个升级门槛都写低于60，后者都写低于100。两种分阶段循环都不能替代现行算法。2025版第一门槛可能使无呼吸或持续60至99次的婴儿未及时获得有效通气；2026版后续门槛又可能在这些心率时过早加按压。现行出生指导把无呼吸、喘息或持续低于100时的辅助通气，与有效通气及纠正后仍持续低于60时的按压分开判断。

00:30:43.704 --> 00:31:20.784
Original threshold check: after the appropriate initial actions, a newly born infant is gasping and the measured heart rate remains92. Do not wait for it to fall below60 before starting indicated useful ventilation, and do not start compressions simply because it is below100. Establish lung inflation and reassess the response using the current birth pathway. Thirty seconds of ineffective bag squeezing is not thirty seconds of effective ventilation. Keep the school reference date visible during rehearsal and ask for the assessed revision rather than inventing a hybrid number.
原创阈值核对：完成适当初步措施后，刚出生婴儿仍喘息，实测心率持续为92。不能等降至60以下才开始有指征的有效通气，也不能只因低于100就按压。应建立肺充气，并按现行出生路径复评反应。三十秒无效挤囊，不等于三十秒有效通气。演练时应注明学校参考日期，核对考核修订版，不能自行拼混合数值。
